            "src": null,
            "widthMm": 70,
            "alt": "Mathematical diagram",
            "overlayOf": null,
            "transparent": false,
            "axes": null,
            "spec": {
              "sourcePage": 29,
              "sourceRegion": "Question 1(b), right",
              "description": "Unticked axes, downward-ended quartic, rising tangent and falling normal meeting at (-1,0).",
              "mathematics": "Curve y=x^2-x^4; tangent y=2x+2; normal y=-x/2-1/2.",
              "answerVisibility": "Supplied curves and lines remain visible; answer equations are omitted."
            },
            "derived": false,
            "reviewStatus": "needs-review"
          }
        ],
        "children": [],
        "diagramPlacement": "right-of-prompt",
        "answer": {
          "short": "Tangent: $y=2x+2$. Normal: $y=-\\frac{x}{2}-\\frac12$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{dy}{dx}&=2x-4x^3\\\\m_{\\mathrm t}&=2(-1)-4(-1)^3\\\\m_{\\mathrm t}&=2\\\\m_{\\mathrm n}&=-\\frac12\\end{align*}$$\nTangent:\n$$\\begin{align*}y-0&=2(x-(-1))\\\\y&=2x+2\\end{align*}$$\nNormal:\n$$\\begin{align*}y-0&=-\\frac12(x-(-1))\\\\y&=-\\frac{x}{2}-\\frac12\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 45
      },
